Rework round 2 on A5 — small, last one. The Scorer passed everything (design fidelity, correctness, conformance, restraint, pass criteria — all independently re-verified, including rebuilding the 92px math from the CSS box model and re-running every gate) except one gap: Completeness.

`zimmDrawer.css.test.ts` only asserts that the new `headerCloseButton` part's *name* exists in the `parts` array — nothing asserts its actual style values, and nothing asserts `prompt.header`'s new `md+` values either. This is the one place this step didn't apply the same rigor as its own sibling fix in the same file — `prompt.content`'s `bottom`/`height`/`maxHeight` values already have exactly this kind of test; this fix's values don't yet.

Add this to `zimmDrawer.css.test.ts`, reusing the existing `stylesAboveMd` helper already in the file:

```ts
describe('ZimmDrawer — headerCloseButton (SFCC-831/689 rework)', () => {
  test('gives the boxed close button a real 44px in-flow row', () => {
    expect(ZimmDrawer.baseStyle.headerCloseButton.height).toBe('2.75rem'); // DRAWER_HEADER_ROW_HEIGHT
  });

  test("prompt's header switches to auto-height/24px padding above md", () => {
    const aboveMd = stylesAboveMd(ZimmDrawer.variants.prompt.header);
    expect(aboveMd.minHeight).toBe('unset');
    expect(aboveMd.paddingBlock).toBe('var(--zimm-scale-xl)'); // HEADER_PADDING_Y
  });
});
```

Per this file's own established method (and this build's standing rule): prove each assertion fails against the pre-fix shape first, then confirm it passes against the current code — don't just add and run once. Adjust the exact values/property names if your read of the current file differs from the Scorer's snippet, but confirm against the real object rather than assuming the snippet is byte-exact.

Re-run `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run test`, `npm run audit:tokens` after — expect file/test count to tick up by exactly 2 tests, everything else unchanged (tsc clean, audit 3 unacknowledged). Report back with the diff and numbers. This is the last round — once this lands we move to commit.

